**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
**1 [[Commander Ostromeda]] spawns after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage plays somewhat like [[Bridge of Forgotten Sporks]]. The start off is generous and stalling it is very helpful. The Doges and the Gory Dark are very susceptible to [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]], while the Sir Rel can be dealt with using some punchier, more fragile units like [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]. As none of the starting enemies spawn infinitely, a well-timed Boulder can be used to leave the field empty. While difficult, this allows for indefinite stalling.

While fighting multiple ostriches is always difficult, M. Ost's combination of [[Knockback]] and [[Slow]] fulfills its usual purpose of keeping your backline away from other pushers. Corporal Weyland's [[Warp]] ends up doing the same, removing all risk from stacking midrangers such as [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]]. By the time Commander Ostromeda arrives it will already be too late: they will be met with a stack large enough to kill them instantly.

Alternatively, crippling M. Ost with [[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Doron]] and [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]] and finishing off the stage with heavier units like [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Uril]] or [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]] is viable too.

==Trivia==
*Obsess-illoscope is a pun on ''obsess'' and ''oscilloscope''.
*Obsess-illoscope's Japanese name, Oshi Rosu Kōpu (推しロス・コープ, "Oshi Los Cope" or "Oshi Ross Cope"), is a pun on 推し ''oshi'' (one's favorite idol, celebrity, character, etc.) and オシロスコープ ''oshirosukōpu'' (oscilloscope), with Los/Ross Cope likely being a fictitious example of a person who is someone else's ''oshi''.

